From 4aefbc184fee1d2a8d658907cfdb84e946753ec2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z-Vibes <180806113+z-Vibes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:48:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] mp: a mods refusal says what the server runs, so the
 client can fetch it

A join refused for mods was a dead end ("mod list does not match"). The
refusal now carries the server's list, and the client hands it to JERICHO's
jer_joinmods, which compares it with the player's saved mod set, checks their
configured mod repos and asks before downloading anything (Download & Join /
No / Keep Them On).

- mp_proto.h: MP_REJECT_MODLIST ('JPMR'), an optional trailer after the
  MP_REJECT of an MP_REJECT_MODS refusal: modCheck, flags (EXACT_SET), count,
  then MP_MOD_INFO rows. No protocol bump: MpHandleReject has always read
  only sizeof(MP_REJECT), so older clients show the refusal as before, and a
  newer client facing an older server finds no tag.
- Listen host: MpSendRejectMods sends its enabled mods without tooling, with
  EXACT_SET (its own rule: the client's set must be the host's).
- Client: MpBeginJoinAsync keeps the address it dialled; MpOfferServerMods
  forwards the rows, MpModIsTooling's ids as `ignore`, and EXACT / EXACT_SET
  to jer_joinmods_offer.
- MpBuildManifest and MpModHash describe what RUNS this boot
  (jer_module_running) instead of what modlist.ini says. They used
  jer_module_list, which ignores -mod / -nomod / -nomods, so a relaunch for a
  server's mods (or -testmode / -mod) told the server the saved set, and it
  refused the very set it had asked for.
- Dedicated server: reject_modlist(cfg) sends mods_match's own requirements
  (core_mods + mods, mod_versions under check 2; EXACT_SET when `mods` is set).
- Python mirror (mp_test.py) and proto_check cover the struct and constants.
- test_plugins.py: the list's contents, bounds and terminators, and that a
  client acting on it is then admitted by mods_match.

Needs the JERICHO core with jer_joinmods.h and jer_module_running.

